bg3le Ext.UI: park the releases of older load generations instead of leaking them

On top of 0001-0004. 0003 leaked every reference Lua let go of in a later UI
generation than it was taken in; the generation moves on at every load, so in
claude-run-2 S015 that was 0 -> 2474 over 4 loads (~600 a load): the client
Lua state is closed at UnloadSession and its boxes are collected during the
load, and what AutoSkip took under the menu and the loading screen is
collected in play. Each is a Noesis object whose refcount never reaches zero,
with whatever it references (children, view models, brushes).

Only a View replacement makes a release unsafe (an element's teardown calls
into its View: 0003's crash). So a reference now also records the View
generation it was taken under (bumped only by "View replaced", once per
launch); those still leak. Everything else from an older load generation, or
let go of while the client is not settled, is parked on the UI thread and
given back once the UI has been settled for 3 s in one generation under the
same View, at most 256 a frame. BG3LE_UI_PARK=0 leaks them as before.

The generation log line now says parked / released late / leaked, and the
leaked classes; Ext._Internal.UiSerialize() returns two more values: parked
now, released late.

Against bg3le 3728a68 (v0.3.6) with 0001-0004. Applied by tools/build_bg3le.sh.
